---
// Published 2 November 2026 for a SURBL delisting request: growthboundmedia.com
// was listed and the sending inboxes on it are benched until it clears.
//
// The copy is Daniel's and is a statement about how he sends. Do not reword it
// to sound better. If how he sends ever changes, this changes with it, because
// the page is only worth anything while it is true.
//
// One sentence was changed the same day, with his say so. It read "individual,
// personally written business correspondence". The sending runs through one
// platform on a campaign schedule, so a reviewer pulling the headers could have
// read that as a denial of something the headers plainly show, and the page
// would have become the problem. "Individually researched and addressed" is the
// same defence and is true of every line in every send.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const updated = '2 November 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Email Policy"
  description={`How ${site.legalName} sends business correspondence, and how to report a concern.`}
  path="/email-policy"
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow label">
        <span>Email Policy</span>
        <span class="head-dim">&middot; Updated {updated}</span>
      </p>
      <h1>Email Policy</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Growthbound does not advertise this website or growthboundmedia.com through
          unsolicited bulk messaging. Any outreach we send is business correspondence,
          individually researched and addressed to publicly published business contact
          addresses, in accordance with the Australian Spam Act 2003. Every message
          identifies the sender and provides direct contact details. Any recipient who
          asks not to be contacted is permanently suppressed. We do not use purchased
          lists, and no affiliate or third party sends messages on our behalf. To report
          a concern: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The other legal pages open with a .short lead block, whose padding is what
     separates the heading from the body. This page is one paragraph, so it has
     to make that gap itself. */
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; margin-top: 22px; }
  .prose p { color: var(--on-dark-soft); margin-bottom: 14px; }
</style>
